  "response": "## Setup\n\nScan output is the 42-finding report above. Verdict run adds:\n\n```json\n\"verdict\": \"unchanged\",\n\"summary\": { \"new\": 0, \"fixed\": 0, \"unchanged\": 42 },\n\"reasons\": [\"no new findings and no fixed findings\"],\n\"recommended_actions\": [\"no maintainability change vs. base — verdict is advisory only.\"]\n```\n\nTwo things that shape the whole plan:\n\n1. **Nothing here is a regression.** All 42 are pre-existing. No gate is failing, so this is scheduled cleanup you sequence for leverage, not a blocker you clear before merging.\n2. **The ranking has no history signal.** `churn`, `recency`, and `blast_radius` are `0` on every one of the 42 findings (the fixture is a symlink to `examples/messy-ts-app` with no independent commit history). So the default ordering is effectively `agent_risk` from local evidence only — **the git-history category is empty, and hotspot weighting is unavailable.** Don't read the top-10 order as \"these files change most.\"\n\n## Top 10, grouped by category\n\nTaking the report's own top 10 (`crime_00001`–`crime_00010`, ranked by `agent_risk` 0.44 → 0.36). Two of your five categories come back empty, and three findings don't fit any of them — noted rather than forced.\n\n| Category | Findings | Response |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Correctness / temporal** *(not in your taxonomy)* | `00001` Temporal Recklessness (high), `00009` Half-UTC Half-Local (high) | **Fix now** |\n| **IA** | `00003` Missing Agent Context, `00006` Route Metadata Drift, `00005` Duplicated Navigation Source | **Fix now** |\n| **Duplication** | `00004` String Sprinkles (`\"enterprise\"` × 4 files) | **Defer** |\n| **Structural** | `00002` Return Shape Roulette, `00008` Option Bag Junk Drawer, `00007` Sync I/O in Hot Path | **Defer** (`00007` rides along — see #4) |\n| **Structural (naming)** | `00010` Negative Flag Maze | **Ignore** |\n| **git-history** | *none in top 10 — none anywhere; churn is 0 across all 42* | n/a |\n| **frontend** | *none in top 10* — `00029` SVG w/ embedded raster (high), `00038`, `00039` sit at #29/#38/#39 | Defer |\n\n## Triage order\n\nBatched by file, because in this repo one pass closes several charges.\n\n**1. `src/date.ts` — fix now.** Clears `00001` + `00009` from the top 10, and off-list `00011` (Timezone Roulette), `00017` (DST-Naive Day Math), `00026`, `00027` — six findings, one file. Both top-10 entries are `severity: high` and the evidence is unambiguous: *\"2× Date.now(), 6× new Date()\"* on lines 4–40, and *\"`d` uses getUTCFullYear() @L9 and getMonth() @L41\"*. The UTC/local mix produces silently wrong output offset by the host timezone; nothing downstream is testable until a clock is injected. Do the clock injection first — it's the precondition for asserting on the rest.\n\n**2. `AGENTS.md` — fix now.** `00003`, `effort: small`, zero behavioural risk, and it's the highest-leverage agent-risk item in the set: *\"package.json declares bin(s): messy — agents have no way to discover commands.\"* Cheapest thing on the list.\n\n**3. The `/settings/billing` naming — fix now.** `00006` and `00005` are the same defect seen twice. Evidence overlaps exactly: component `PricingPage`, `metadata.title: Plans`, `<title>: Subscription`, nav label `Plans` in `registry.ts`, `Billing` in `sidebar.ts`. Pick one canonical name, derive the rest. One decision, two findings cleared, and it de-risks the three Orphaned Destination findings (`00034`–`00036`) you'll want to look at next.\n\n**4. `src/api/files.ts` — fix now (bundled).** `00007` is only `severity: low` on its own and I'd normally defer it — but the same file carries `00015` (`localhost:3000` @L8) and `00016` (`/Users/andrew/dev/crimes/schema.json` @L9), both `effort: quick` and both of which break on every machine that isn't yours. You're opening the file anyway; swap the three `*Sync` calls while you're there.\n\n**5. `\"enterprise\"` literal — defer.** `00004` spans `src/api/plan.ts`, `src/billing.ts`, `src/jobs/plan-sync.ts`, `src/ui/pricing.ts`, and crimes rates the fix `risk: medium`. It wants a home module that doesn't exist yet. Defer until the billing split (see below) gives it one — doing it now means picking an arbitrary location you'll move later.\n\n**6. `src/petty.ts` contracts — defer.** `00002` and `00008` are both real (*\"lowest key overlap: 0%\"*; *\"6 distinct property reads: currency, plan, region, retry, role, status\"*), both `severity: low`, and both are typing work with no behavioural payoff. One batched pass, later.\n\n**7. `00010` Negative Flag Maze — ignore.** `severity: 0.25`, two flags, one condition: `!disableBilling && !skipRetry`. A rename touches call sites for no correctness gain. If you want it out of the report permanently rather than just unscheduled:\n\n```bash\ncrimes feedback negative_flag_maze::src/petty.ts::::9361fc296993 \\\n  --verdict fp --note \"Two-flag condition, single call site — rename cost exceeds the clarity gain\"\n```\n\n## One caveat on the top 10\n\nThe default ordering is `agent_risk`, and with `churn`/`blast_radius` pinned at 0 it's dominated by local readability signals. Three findings with the highest raw severity in the report fall *outside* the top 10:\n\n- `00033` Contract Split-Brain — `Invoice` — `severity: 0.96`, **6 field disagreements** including `currency`, `subtotalCents`, `taxCents`, `discountCents` between `src/api/state.ts:9` and `src/billing.ts:19`. Money fields disagreeing across two live declarations with *\"nothing in the build checks the two declarations against each other.\"* This is the most consequential defect in the repo and it ranks #33.\n- `00032` Contract Split-Brain — `User` — `severity: 0.90`, same pattern, one field.\n- `00014` God Function `generateInvoice` — `severity: 0.90`, 204 lines, 3.4× threshold.\n\n**Recommendation: promote `00033` and `00032` into the fix-now band, directly after step 1.** Unify the two declarations before anyone edits billing — that also gives step 5's `\"enterprise\"` literal somewhere principled to live. Leave `00014` deferred; per the auto-fix policy, don't split a God Function as a drive-by, and the weak tests protecting it (`00025`: *\"0 expect/assert calls\"*) mean you'd be refactoring without a net.",
